Status: done. The task stays `[~]`, because the r2 rebuild (Task 2.9 part 1) follows in the next role.

The fault: the Task 2.9 part 1 build printed the student back with the heading "Story" and no text
under it. `questPanelValues` built its own book row, and that row held an empty story text. The
guard of the build refused only a fully empty panel, so an empty story passed.

The fix, in `questPanelValues(level, unit)`:
1. It now reads the book row of that level and unit from `content/storytime/covers/books.json`
   through `loadStorytimeCoverBooks` and the constant `STORYTIME_COVER_BOOKS_FILE` of
   `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/covers.ts` (read-only import, spec D-A2).
2. It passes that row's panel (the story text and its weeks, and the four week lists) to
   `storytimeCoverPanelValues`. A missing row is an error.
3. It refuses an empty panel field. An empty value pushes "the student back panel field <field> is
   empty; the build refuses an empty field" and returns no values (the A-F1 form).
4. The JSDoc names the new source and the new gate for the caller.

No committed Red test changed. No shared file changed. No test file changed.

